{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/views/thread.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.120298Z","id":"bec7903625993bb5a00707b1697df5ef14856c0591212b8b6de989978f07975a","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/views/thread.rs:944-988, record da32124b.\n\nMoved from crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs:1569-1613, record e7b6d312.\n\nSpec §8.3 gives a thread withheld: {count, authors, approval} whenever any field is withheld but does not say what count counts. Withhold::thread counts withheld comments (the number the feedback line and approval requests speak of), so a thread whose only withheld field is its anchor, clip, resolved_by or a batch note has count 0.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:3cadd457","span":{"start":{"line":1028},"end":{"line":1072},"content_hash":"472a63a615cac43e0ca525689a793d0aab4ecaadecaaef4ad8767556155767a4"},"summary":"A thread's withheld.count counts its withheld comment bodies only","supersedes":"1a8bf7f609fa2843ad7ea2c78f0d7e02e729dda6bc1aada767b7882995df7c39","tags":["visibility","spec:8.3","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/views/thread.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.165144Z","id":"c81a3c9a59d131b6a53205dc61d48ce486097b8d9da68489dc9d0cbc9ab21e68","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs:1705-1749, record b6bcda05.\n\nSpec §8.3 gives a thread withheld: {count, authors, approval} whenever any field is withheld but does not say what count counts. Withhold::thread counts withheld comments (the number the feedback line and approval requests speak of), so a thread whose only withheld field is its anchor, clip, resolved_by or a batch note has count 0.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:27b591eb5eb290f789cd5f959845f6d1064768a7","span":{"start":{"line":1028},"end":{"line":1072},"content_hash":"472a63a615cac43e0ca525689a793d0aab4ecaadecaaef4ad8767556155767a4"},"summary":"A thread's withheld.count counts its withheld comment bodies only","tags":["visibility","spec:8.3","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/views/thread.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.165202Z","id":"34ad716e093fb558fb7d5e946104a2f9364cfa06586c0f4b893da01b2c99562e","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs:1823-1850, record ba1e86e0.\n\nWithhold::approval runs Store::request_state once per thread that withholds anything, so a listing of N such threads makes N indexed reads (plus st.owner() when the owner is withheld). Versions and names are cached per call. vis_threads_ms (Task 25) will show whether it matters.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:27b591eb5eb290f789cd5f959845f6d1064768a7","span":{"start":{"line":1146},"end":{"line":1173},"content_hash":"05c56d201c29c0092d6039e9c09166c4bdf07ea63e935e45f87326bf15b12593"},"summary":"Each thread with withheld content costs one approval_requests query in a listing","tags":["perf","visibility","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/views/thread.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:45:32.427970Z","id":"921e8820c45702030927321e8e8398e41cda42ed03a3cab6f07a82eace77ac45","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"The same record as bec79036 at crates/clax-http/src/views/thread.rs:1028, kept: this head is a re-anchor of it made on a branch while main moved it there","supersedes":"c81a3c9a59d131b6a53205dc61d48ce486097b8d9da68489dc9d0cbc9ab21e68","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/views/approval.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:07:28.797540Z","id":"dee628740348f7e22f4e7c908c989e8850a0d2fd526a8f8d0639027418a79c60","body":{"detail":"views::approval::card is synchronous inside a store job, while the documents an author holds come from the artifact's store through the async host (AppDataOp::AuthoredBy). The inbox routes (crates/clax-server/src/routes/inbox.rs) and the inbox listener (crates/clax-http/src/views/inbox.rs) call fill_card_docs on what they answer; it recognises a card by a null thread_id and a content holding docs and files arrays. Each such card costs one host call.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":224},"end":{"line":279},"content_hash":"e4a21fdc926eea891e62cfd6a7793624663e3bf0e2774f2f1375cfd4796b3401"},"summary":"An approval card's docs are filled after its view is rendered, by walking the JSON (fill_card_docs); a route that renders cards without calling it shows an empty docs list","tags":["deferred-work","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/views/thread.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:13:08.379Z","id":"ae807d3bdb744bd1bca0742c63d5021631398b9aeecd8ef78dcb3c3faf02d3b7","body":{"detail":"Failure: Ada publishes an app and shares it with Sam at Can edit (or Can view); Sam's Clax app, signed in with kind clax-app, reads it through its core (crates/clax-server/src/routes/remote_apps.rs). GET /api/artifacts/<id>/head answers title null and content_sha256 null (bundle.content_sha256 null too), GET .../versions/1/bundle answers 403 withheld ('this version holds files withheld until your person approves their authors'), and GET .../versions/1/files/index.html 403 withheld, because VisFor::of filters every agent caller for its reader and a person-device grant is an agent grant. The app's RemoteHead.fromJson (apps/clax_app/lib/remote/models.dart) casts title as a String, so Get my apps and every pull of a shared app fail with bad_response; an editor's publish also cannot see the base version's withheld paths to remove them (crates/clax-server/src/public.rs push_app). Seen by probing in crates/clax-server/tests/api_remotes_app.rs editor_pull_then_push_publishes_as_editor, which therefore builds the editor's local copy without reading the files. Options: read a person-device grant as its person (Caller::Person-like visibility) on the artifact read routes, or have the person approve the authors once, from the app.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":405},"end":{"line":419},"content_hash":"db102f5cb86062c53e4f48489f0042f990abecba3e6142d0d50bb5cb161d78e2"},"summary":"A person's own device (a clax-app token) reads another person's shared app as an agent channel: its head, bundle and files are withheld","tags":["app-push","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/views/thread.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:58:52.214207Z","id":"9b16bccdd81c14d94305b9564540e151a189bd5825d961c473a7093b43bd52f1","body":{"detail":"Probe (scratch lines in api_remotes_app::editor_pull_then_push_publishes_as_editor after Sam's library read, reverted): Sam's core GET .../head 200 with title null, content_sha256 null, bundle.content_sha256 null; GET .../versions/1/bundle 403 withheld; GET .../versions/1/files/index.html 403 withheld (authors [Ada]); GET .../versions/1/files 200 with files {} and files_withheld 1. Deciding code: crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs verify_layer (around 2039) gives a person-device grant the person's identity (PersonDevice) only on PERSON_DEVICE_ROUTES (agent.rs 1751-1758: sharing and /api/hosted/apps); every artifact read route falls to the ordinary grant path, crates/clax-http/src/identity.rs 332-338 makes it Caller::PersonAgent { person: Some(p) }, Caller::reader (crates/clax-http/src/auth.rs 62-72) returns Reader::Person(p), and VisFor::of (views/thread.rs 408-418) filters it with Visibility::for_reader, which withholds authors the person has not approved. Smallest change: add GET /api/artifacts/{aid}/head, GET /api/artifacts/{aid}/versions/{n}, GET /api/artifacts/{aid}/versions/{n}/bundle and GET /api/artifacts/{aid}/versions/{n}/files/{*path} to PERSON_DEVICE_ROUTES, and have the caller of a request carrying PersonDevice resolve as Caller::Person { viewer } (the person's browser), so VisFor has no reader; whether a device reads unfiltered is the owner's call.","kind":"comment","references":"ae807d3bdb744bd1bca0742c63d5021631398b9aeecd8ef78dcb3c3faf02d3b7","summary":"Confirmed by probe and code trace: a clax-app device token reads another person's shared app as that person's agent channel","tags":["session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/views/thread.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T17:04:05.400524Z","id":"3bd0c8d7044074191d589ce7502f76b52bd95eb2097a8143ebda6da31d322f1b","body":{"detail":"PERSON_DEVICE_ROUTES (crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs) now holds GET /api/artifacts/{aid}/head, /versions/{n}, /versions/{n}/bundle and /versions/{n}/files/{*path}; Identity::caller (crates/clax-http/src/identity.rs) resolves a request carrying PersonDevice as Caller::Person (Caller::Owner for the owner's device), and Agent takes MemberRights::of_session for it, so the person's rights and link access limit it as they limit the browser. Every other route still refuses a device; a plain agent token still reads filtered. api_remotes_app::a_device_reads_shared_apps_as_its_person (bazel test //crates/clax-server:integration__6) checks head title and hashes, bundle and files through Sam's core, a plain agent token of Sam's still withheld (403), and a revoked device 401; it fails at api_remotes_app.rs:1316 (title null) with the Identity device branch disabled.","kind":"comment","references":"ae807d3bdb744bd1bca0742c63d5021631398b9aeecd8ef78dcb3c3faf02d3b7","summary":"Owner's decision: \"Same as browser\" — a person's Clax app device reads shared apps exactly as that person's browser session does. Done in git:8a6af1251; close is the owner's.","tags":["session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/views/thread.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:57:34.733129Z","id":"61e32f1e6873f0284ca4e9d7be7197b0e499a5b6399ff467f6b28395e34be406","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"ae807d3bdb744bd1bca0742c63d5021631398b9aeecd8ef78dcb3c3faf02d3b7","summary":"End-to-end tests pin this: crates/clax-server/tests/app_push_pull_e2e.rs a_viewer_pulls_and_is_offered_the_republished_bundle is #[ignore]d on it and fails at its head[\"title\"] assertion (left: Null, right: \"Tips\") under --include-ignored; un-ignore it with the fix. Its sibling publish_pull_republish_update_then_web_edit_moves, and apps/clax_app/test/remote/push_pull_real_test.dart, take the app on the owner's own second device, which this does not affect, so neither covers a recipient who is another person.","tags":["session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/views/thread.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T17:16:30.210102Z","id":"b9c397546ade8a700835e9e8be467423a712ff15b133a2cff6864c4b6627629e","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"ae807d3bdb744bd1bca0742c63d5021631398b9aeecd8ef78dcb3c3faf02d3b7","summary":"The app side of the owner's decision: before Claude first reads an app written by someone else, the Clax app asks once per app and author (sheet 'Claude reads what <author> wrote', Continue or Cancel; apps/clax_app/lib/agent/author_trust.dart, lib/ui/author_trust_sheet.dart, gated in lib/app.dart _gateRun; git:0eea2df38 on akesling/app-pp-d). Merges of another publisher's version are gated the same way (record 0cd688b2).","tags":["session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/views/thread.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T19:23:17.970864Z","id":"d0d4de6306b1848fe032e19e21109e75248d5d5f15fd2210ca25bb2babd35f07","body":{"detail":"GET /api/artifacts/{aid}/threads, /threads/{tid} and /threads/{tid}/clip are in PERSON_DEVICE_ROUTES (crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs), and the list takes since from a device (crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs list). api_linked::a_members_device_brings_down_a_strangers_comment (bazel test //crates/clax-server:integration__5): a member's app, Comments on, shared with Bob at Can comment; Bob's browser comment comes down to her core with its text; it fails at api_linked.rs:2302 (no thread) with the three routes removed. The local core does not withhold such mirrored strangers from its own agents; that is the open blocker on crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs insert_mirrored.","kind":"comment","references":"ae807d3bdb744bd1bca0742c63d5021631398b9aeecd8ef78dcb3c3faf02d3b7","summary":"Extended to threads, by the owner's same decision for comments: \"Same as browser\". Done in git:afcdea2f2; close is the owner's.","tags":["session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/views/thread.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:38:52.495836Z","id":"5efaf6b5a5562fa9ce07efe1870ee6ca10cc1f5871e729ae1e6f0696bc8645ac","body":{"detail":"Failure: Ada publishes an app and shares it with Sam at Can edit (or Can view); Sam's Clax app, signed in with kind clax-app, reads it through its core (crates/clax-server/src/routes/remote_apps.rs). GET /api/artifacts/<id>/head answers title null and content_sha256 null (bundle.content_sha256 null too), GET .../versions/1/bundle answers 403 withheld ('this version holds files withheld until your person approves their authors'), and GET .../versions/1/files/index.html 403 withheld, because VisFor::of filters every agent caller for its reader and a person-device grant is an agent grant. The app's RemoteHead.fromJson (apps/clax_app/lib/remote/models.dart) casts title as a String, so Get my apps and every pull of a shared app fail with bad_response; an editor's publish also cannot see the base version's withheld paths to remove them (crates/clax-server/src/public.rs push_app). Seen by probing in crates/clax-server/tests/api_remotes_app.rs editor_pull_then_push_publishes_as_editor, which therefore builds the editor's local copy without reading the files. Options: read a person-device grant as its person (Caller::Person-like visibility) on the artifact read routes, or have the person approve the authors once, from the app.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":405},"end":{"line":419},"content_hash":"1c3253e54862ec3dff9ecb3a6654a81bab37e76ce5b6024e09228f0e6a675c25"},"summary":"A person's own device (a clax-app token) reads another person's shared app as an agent channel: its head, bundle and files are withheld","supersedes":"ae807d3bdb744bd1bca0742c63d5021631398b9aeecd8ef78dcb3c3faf02d3b7","tags":["app-push","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/views/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T19:34:25.879046Z","id":"a1ad90d9ab83322171bcbe7224f5e4f5eb93a5da6b7c2efe2a0598189f500589","body":{"detail":"out_of_reach runs Store::inbox_artifacts (one DISTINCT scan of the recipient's items) and then MemberRights::lists per artifact (Store::reach and, beyond reach, the share rights) on every inbox list, summary, item read, mark, agent strip, GET /api/agents and inbox event batch on a hosted daemon. An owner whose inbox names thousands of artifacts pays thousands of point reads per request.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":150},"end":{"line":175},"content_hash":"3c901ea487553634b9d1e820e39890866fdfea2d0dcdd11881010abe5c068911"},"suggested_fix":"Keep the hidden set per recipient keyed by the visibility generation and the shares' change count, or push the reach rule into the inbox SQL (artifacts.person and the shares table) instead of an ID list.","summary":"Every hosted inbox read scans the recipient's inbox artifacts and reads each one's reach","tags":["hosted","perf","revisit:an inbox read over 50 ms in just perf on a hosted home","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/views/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T23:23:30.699030Z","id":"a22caa78e93d672e7042968b498a3dc41ee7cd375fa174e125c4ecc1ed5754df","body":{"detail":"out_of_reach (crates/clax-http/src/views/inbox.rs:150) feeds Store::list_questions_leaving_out in GET /api/questions and GET /api/inbox/summary (crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs list, crates/clax-server/src/routes/inbox.rs summary), so each pays inbox_artifacts plus one MemberRights::lists per artifact in the recipient's inbox history, not only those on the page returned.","kind":"comment","references":"a1ad90d9ab83322171bcbe7224f5e4f5eb93a5da6b7c2efe2a0598189f500589","suggested_fix":"Join the reach in SQL: artifacts.person IS NULL OR artifacts.person = ?recipient, or an artifact in the recipient's shares (with the granted rights' locations applied in Rust only to the rows returned), instead of evaluating lists over the whole history.","summary":"The same scan now also runs before every question list and inbox summary, and on each inbox announcement","tags":["session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/views/thread.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T23:51:44.276144Z","id":"8d58a2b384c8a008b6616d035cc808e034f442b05276f5b301e9ed56225f9b98","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/views/thread.rs:944-988, record da32124b.\n\nMoved from crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs:1569-1613, record e7b6d312.\n\nSpec §8.3 gives a thread withheld: {count, authors, approval} whenever any field is withheld but does not say what count counts. Withhold::thread counts withheld comments (the number the feedback line and approval requests speak of), so a thread whose only withheld field is its anchor, clip, resolved_by or a batch note has count 0.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-http/src/views/thread.rs:1028:1072 to crates/clax-http/src/views/thread.rs:1025:1069: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1025},"end":{"line":1069},"content_hash":"472a63a615cac43e0ca525689a793d0aab4ecaadecaaef4ad8767556155767a4"},"summary":"A thread's withheld.count counts its withheld comment bodies only","supersedes":"bec7903625993bb5a00707b1697df5ef14856c0591212b8b6de989978f07975a","tags":["visibility","spec:8.3","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/views/thread.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T23:51:44.325223Z","id":"dbe5207d1c4de4051a9c91eb18aca6458a800efbfe7fb0cd4030a1ae5e816771","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs:1823-1850, record ba1e86e0.\n\nWithhold::approval runs Store::request_state once per thread that withholds anything, so a listing of N such threads makes N indexed reads (plus st.owner() when the owner is withheld). Versions and names are cached per call. vis_threads_ms (Task 25) will show whether it matters.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-http/src/views/thread.rs:1146:1173 to crates/clax-http/src/views/thread.rs:1143:1170: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1143},"end":{"line":1170},"content_hash":"05c56d201c29c0092d6039e9c09166c4bdf07ea63e935e45f87326bf15b12593"},"summary":"Each thread with withheld content costs one approval_requests query in a listing","supersedes":"34ad716e093fb558fb7d5e946104a2f9364cfa06586c0f4b893da01b2c99562e","tags":["perf","visibility","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/views/thread.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-24T01:44:08.134067Z","id":"abcebd2dca4ddfbf009758bad0a03b9303f656f0a2f2dc74ee25298a9dc8a708","body":{"detail":"Failure: Ada publishes an app and shares it with Sam at Can edit (or Can view); Sam's Clax app, signed in with kind clax-app, reads it through its core (crates/clax-server/src/routes/remote_apps.rs). GET /api/artifacts/<id>/head answers title null and content_sha256 null (bundle.content_sha256 null too), GET .../versions/1/bundle answers 403 withheld ('this version holds files withheld until your person approves their authors'), and GET .../versions/1/files/index.html 403 withheld, because VisFor::of filters every agent caller for its reader and a person-device grant is an agent grant. The app's RemoteHead.fromJson (apps/clax_app/lib/remote/models.dart) casts title as a String, so Get my apps and every pull of a shared app fail with bad_response; an editor's publish also cannot see the base version's withheld paths to remove them (crates/clax-server/src/public.rs push_app). Seen by probing in crates/clax-server/tests/api_remotes_app.rs editor_pull_then_push_publishes_as_editor, which therefore builds the editor's local copy without reading the files. Options: read a person-device grant as its person (Caller::Person-like visibility) on the artifact read routes, or have the person approve the authors once, from the app.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":402},"end":{"line":416},"content_hash":"db102f5cb86062c53e4f48489f0042f990abecba3e6142d0d50bb5cb161d78e2"},"summary":"A person's own device (a clax-app token) reads another person's shared app as an agent channel: its head, bundle and files are withheld","supersedes":"ae807d3bdb744bd1bca0742c63d5021631398b9aeecd8ef78dcb3c3faf02d3b7","tags":["app-push","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/views/thread.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-24T01:44:08.201533Z","id":"8e48b9e9d45dae6a74cb90f63850f2d9eafa24fb6cbe15c488b02b96b56f1514","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/views/thread.rs:944-988, record da32124b.\n\nMoved from crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs:1569-1613, record e7b6d312.\n\nSpec §8.3 gives a thread withheld: {count, authors, approval} whenever any field is withheld but does not say what count counts. Withhold::thread counts withheld comments (the number the feedback line and approval requests speak of), so a thread whose only withheld field is its anchor, clip, resolved_by or a batch note has count 0.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-http/src/views/thread.rs:1028:1072 to crates/clax-http/src/views/thread.rs:1025:1069: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1040},"end":{"line":1084},"content_hash":"472a63a615cac43e0ca525689a793d0aab4ecaadecaaef4ad8767556155767a4"},"summary":"A thread's withheld.count counts its withheld comment bodies only","supersedes":"8d58a2b384c8a008b6616d035cc808e034f442b05276f5b301e9ed56225f9b98","tags":["visibility","spec:8.3","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
