{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/views/thread.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-24T14:57:10.189377Z","id":"014ecc1f954710bd1df5910bfd9a1ffdad4424c8975534a05a831dc5660adbe4","body":{"detail":"Failure: Ada publishes an app and shares it with Sam at Can edit (or Can view); Sam's Clax app, signed in with kind clax-app, reads it through its core (crates/clax-server/src/routes/remote_apps.rs). GET /api/artifacts/<id>/head answers title null and content_sha256 null (bundle.content_sha256 null too), GET .../versions/1/bundle answers 403 withheld ('this version holds files withheld until your person approves their authors'), and GET .../versions/1/files/index.html 403 withheld, because VisFor::of filters every agent caller for its reader and a person-device grant is an agent grant. The app's RemoteHead.fromJson (apps/clax_app/lib/remote/models.dart) casts title as a String, so Get my apps and every pull of a shared app fail with bad_response; an editor's publish also cannot see the base version's withheld paths to remove them (crates/clax-server/src/public.rs push_app). Seen by probing in crates/clax-server/tests/api_remotes_app.rs editor_pull_then_push_publishes_as_editor, which therefore builds the editor's local copy without reading the files. Options: read a person-device grant as its person (Caller::Person-like visibility) on the artifact read routes, or have the person approve the authors once, from the app.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":401},"end":{"line":415},"content_hash":"db102f5cb86062c53e4f48489f0042f990abecba3e6142d0d50bb5cb161d78e2"},"summary":"A person's own device (a clax-app token) reads another person's shared app as an agent channel: its head, bundle and files are withheld","supersedes":"abcebd2dca4ddfbf009758bad0a03b9303f656f0a2f2dc74ee25298a9dc8a708","tags":["app-push","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
